/*! @brief Buffered read object

 The BufferedStream object is a buffered stream object for binary stream reading. It can cache the underlying stream and provide text reading capabilities. When using the BufferedStream object, you only need to pass the stream object to be processed as a constructor parameter. Creation method:
 ```JavaScript
 var reader = new io.BufferedStream(stream);
 ```

 BufferedStream inherits from the Stream object and has all the methods and properties of the Stream object. The stream property is used to query the stream object when creating the cache object. The BufferedStream object also supports the EOL property for querying and setting the line ending identifier (default: posix:\"\n\"; windows:\"\r\n\") and the charset property for querying and setting the character set when the current object processes text, default is utf-8.

 When reading stream data, the BufferedStream object uses a chunked approach, first reading the data into the buffer, and then obtaining the data from the buffer, which can effectively reduce the number of network interactions when reading stream data and improve reading efficiency.

 The BufferedStream object also provides a write method to write the given data to the stream, and when the underlying stream object is in write blocking, it waits for it to accept data before proceeding to the next operation. The Flush method writes the file buffer content to the physical device. The close method closes the current stream object. Some methods can be implemented in subclasses.

 When using the BufferedStream object, be careful not to mix it with other underlying stream objects that are already in use, otherwise it may cause data to be read repeatedly or read errors.

 Below is an example code for reading file content using the BufferedStream object:
  ```JavaScript
  var fs = require('fs');
  var io = require('io');

  var filename = "test.txt";

  // open file
  var file = fs.openFile(filename);

  // create BufferedStream object
  var reader = new io.BufferedStream(file);

  // read file content
  var lines = reader.readLines();

  for(var i = 0; i < lines.length; i ++)
      console.log(lines[i]);

  // close file
  file.close();
  ```
 */
interface BufferedStream : Stream
{
    /*! @brief BufferedStream constructor
      @param stm BufferedStream's binary base stream object
     */
    BufferedStream(Stream stm);

    /*! @brief Reads text of specified characters
     @param size Specifies the number of text characters to read, based on utf8 or specified encoding bytes
     @return Returns the read text string, returns null if no data is readable or the connection is interrupted
     */
    String readText(Integer size) async;

    /*! @brief Reads one line of text, line ending identifier based on EOL property setting, default: posix:\"\\n\"; windows:\"\\r\\n\"
     @param maxlen Specifies the maximum string for this read, based on utf8 encoded bytes, default no limit on characters
     @return Returns the read text string, returns null if no data is readable or the connection is interrupted
     */
    String readLine(Integer maxlen = -1) async;

    /*! @brief Reads a group of text lines as an array, line ending identifier based on EOL property setting, default: posix:\"\\n\"; windows:\"\\r\\n\"
     @param maxlines Specifies the maximum number of lines to read this time, default reads all text lines
     @return Returns the read text line array, empty array if no data is readable or the connection is interrupted
     */
    Array readLines(Integer maxlines = -1);

    /*! @brief Reads a text string ending with the specified bytes
     @param mk Specifies the ending string
     @param maxlen Specifies the maximum string for this read, based on utf8 encoded bytes, default no limit on characters
     @return Returns the read text string, returns null if no data is readable or the connection is interrupted
     */
    String readUntil(String mk, Integer maxlen = -1) async;

    /*! @brief Writes a string
     @param txt Specifies the string to write
     @return The actual number of bytes written
     */
    Integer writeText(String txt) async;

    /*! @brief Writes a string and writes a newline character
     @param txt Specifies the string to write
     @return The actual number of bytes written
     */
    Integer writeLine(String txt) async;

    /*! @brief Queries the stream object when creating the cache object */
    readonly Stream stream;

    /*! @brief Queries and sets the character set when the current object processes text, default is utf-8 */
    String charset;

    /*! @brief Queries and sets the line ending identifier, default: posix:\"\\n\"; windows:\"\\r\\n\"   */
    String EOL;
};